<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-guatemala"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Guatemala.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Guatemala</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Peace accords end thirty-six years of internal armed conflict</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/new-zealand"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/New%20Zealand.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>New Zealand</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">First election under mixed-member proportional representation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-china"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20China.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of China</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">First direct presidential election, won by Lee Teng-hui</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-south-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20South%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of South Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A new constitution with a Bill of Rights is adopted</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/luddites"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Luddites.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Luddites</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A Second Luddite Congress at Barnesville, Ohio, issues a manifesto of neo-Luddism</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/kabul"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kabul.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kabul</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Taliban seize Kabul</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/buenos-aires"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Buenos%20Aires.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Buenos Aires</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The city elects its first head of government, after the constitutional amendment of 1994 gave it autonomy</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/pan-islamism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Islamism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Islamism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Necmettin Erbakan founds the Developing 8 Countries</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/mohism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mohism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mohism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Jin Guantao, Fan Hongye and Liu Qingfeng argue that Chinese science lacked a definitive structure without a flourishing Mohism</span></li></ul></section>
